abstract: >-
  This monograph presents a formal reconstruction of the Indus (Harappan) 
  script as an operational symbolic system implementing finite mathematics, 
  relational logic, and state-based validation. This work does NOT propose 
  a phonetic decipherment, but rather analyzes the script as a formal system 
  of operational notation used for administrative and institutional validation.
  The reconstruction includes finite arithmetic, cardinal operations, relational 
  logic, state transitions, and institutional validation mechanisms, with formal 
  equivalents expressed in modern computational terms.
title: "Indus Operational Mathematics: A Formal Framework for State-Based Symbol Systems"
